{"availability":"available","full":"OceanGlidersCommunity/glidertest","name":"glidertest","description":"Diagnostic test of glider data quality and required processing","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":2,"forks":10,"created":"2024-06-12T15:25:39Z","updated":"2026-10-16T08:37:19Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://oceangliderscommunity.github.io/glidertest/","topics":["oceanography","underwater-glider"],"demo":"https://oceangliderscommunity.github.io/glidertest/_static/demo/index.html","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T21:32:25.303Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T21:32:25.303Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T21:32:25.303Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T23:20:29.814Z","stars":2,"forks":10},{"at":"2026-10-16T21:32:25.303Z","stars":2,"forks":10}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["glidertest reads an OceanGliders (OG1) mission file, runs a set of diagnostics on it, and shows you what is in the file. It never modifies, fixes or grids the data: the output is figures and an HTML report, the input file is left untouched. It works one mission at a time; a fleet page links the reports of many missions on one map.","There are two ways to use it: call the diagnostic functions from a notebook (glidertest.plots, glidertest.tools), or run glidertest report on a file and read the HTML."],"features":["Time and depth spacing","Histograms and T–S diagrams","Suspect profile durations","Dive–climb bias (the difference between down and up profiles)","Non-photochemical quenching in chlorophyll"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/OceanGlidersCommunity/glidertest/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"c7c58baef386a0c5024b7e68760f65d7d34afe4cded9cc086bffe92788430bbe","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T23:20:29.916Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T23:20:29.916Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"glidertest reads an OceanGliders (OG1) mission file, runs a set of diagnostics on it, and s